\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Markov Chain Text Generator\
\
## Project Overview\
This project implements a simple text generator using a **Markov Chain**.  \
It predicts the next word based on the previous word(s) using a statistical model.\
\
\
## Tools Used\
- Python 3\
- Standard libraries: `random`, `re`\
\
\
\
## How It Works\
1. A text dataset is used as training data.\
2. The text is preprocessed:\
   - Converted to lowercase\
   - Punctuation removed\
   - Split into words\
3. A Markov Chain dictionary is created where each word points to possible next words.\
4. New text is generated by randomly choosing the next word from the dictionary.\
\
\
\
## Training Text Sample\
Cybersecurity is important for protecting data.\
Cybersecurity helps prevent cyber attacks.\
Data protection is essential.\
\
\
## Example Output\
cybersecurity is important for protecting data protection is essential\
\
\
\
## Comparison with GPT-2\
\
| Markov Chain | GPT-2 |\
|--------------|-------|\
| Rule-based | Deep learning |\
| Small memory | Large neural network |\
| Simple probabilities | Context-aware |\
| Easy to implement | Complex |\
\
\
## Conclusion\
This project demonstrates how a Markov Chain can generate text using word transition probabilities.  \
It is simple, beginner-friendly, and a good introduction to probabilistic text generation.\
\
